<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Zahrawi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 936–1013</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Abulcasis, Abu al-Qasim al-Zahrawi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Zahrawi, known in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> as Abulcasis, was a physician of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> who worked at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> and is regarded as one of the greatest surgeons of the medieval world. His medical encyclopedia, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kitob">Kitab</a> al-Tasrif, ends with a treatise on surgery describing operations and illustrating some two hundred instruments. Translated into Latin by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerard-of-cremona">Gerard of Cremona</a>, it was used in European medicine for centuries.</p></div>
